  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Preheat the oven to 220C. Line an oven tray with baking paper. Cut the unpeeled sweet potato into 2cm-thick wedges. Thinly slice the onion. Slice the tomato.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/459159/photos/large/73496_1-5d31a7dca12a1d14fe3845f6f4d6ad75.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Roast wedges: Put the sweet potato and onion on the lined tray. Drizzle with 2 tsp olive oil, sprinkle with the Caribbean seasoning, season with salt and pepper and toss to coat. Roast for 20-25 mins until golden and tender.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/459160/photos/large/73496_2-ee50bfa398e6a99e155b3b8dcd6a2fb5.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Warm patties: Meanwhile, heat 1 tbs olive oil in a medium frypan over high heat (see Kitchen 101). Reduce the heat to medium-high and cook the veggie patties for 3-4 mins each side until golden. Remove from the pan.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/459161/photos/large/73496_3-010835654ba5891960d9a070fd4def6e.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fry eggs and toast rolls: Heat 2 tsp olive oil in the same pan over medium heat. Crack 2 eggs into the pan and cook for 3-4 mins until just set or cooked to your liking. Meanwhile, cut the rolls in half. Put on an oven tray, cut side up, and bake for 5-6 mins until lightly toasted.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/459162/photos/large/73496_4-dc2c190af8a90d62eca6b8d5183069e0.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Spread the roll bases with mayonnaise and top with the spinach, patties, tomato, egg and onion. Drizzle with tomato sauce, if using, and serve with the sweet potato wedges. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/459163/photos/large/73496_5-68ad01c00b67ddb23f7848b2b2cdfd44.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kitchen 101: It's important to have the pan very hot before adding the patties, then cook one side at a time, rather than turning regularly, to prevent them from breaking up.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/459164/photos/large/73496_6-b25d45e4c487777bd6ff5b92acaa234b.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
